lesson: 220
title: Riders on tandems and bicycles
level: primary-4
stars: 2
explain: A tandem is a bicycle made for two: it has 2 seats, one behind the other, and 2 wheels like an ordinary bicycle.
explain: If some riders are on full tandems and the rest ride a bicycle each, first find how many ride alone.
explain: 13 riders, 4 full tandems: 4 × 2 = 8 ride tandems, 13 − 8 = 5 ride bicycles, so 4 + 5 = 9 cycles and 9 × 2 = 18 wheels.
vars: a=name t=2..6 b=2..9 z=2..8
let: r = t * 2 + b
answer: (t + b) * 2
exercise: {r} riders go on a cycle tour. {t} tandems are full and every other rider has a bicycle. How many wheels are on the tour?
exercise: {a}'s club has {r} riders out today: they fill {t} tandems and the rest ride bicycles on their own. How many wheels are rolling?
exercise: At the seaside {r} people hire cycles. {t} tandems go out full, and everyone else takes a bicycle. How many wheels do the hired cycles have?
exercise: {r} children ride in the park. Some fill {t} tandems and the others ride a bicycle each. How many wheels are there?
exercise: How many wheels carry {r} riders if {t} full tandems carry some of them and each of the others is on a bicycle?
exercise: {r} of us cycling, {t} tandems full, rest on bikes. how many wheels
exercise: bike hire: {r} ppl, {t} tandems all full, everyone else own bike. wheels?
exercise: {a} reckons {r} riders means {r*2} wheels. nope, {t} tandems full, rest on bikes. how many wheels
exercise: {r} riders — {t+1} tandems, sorry {t} tandems, full — the others on bikes. how many wheels
exercise: tour: {r} riders, {z} water stops lol, {t} tandems full n rest on bicycles. wheels total
exercise: There are {r} cyclists. {t} tandems are full and the others ride bicycles. How many wheels are there?
test: Every rider of a group of {r} is either on one of {t} full tandems or alone on a bicycle. How many wheels does the group have?
test: How many tyres need pumping before {r} riders set off, if {t} tandems are full and all the others ride bicycles?
test: A tandem-and-bicycle race starts with {r} riders: {t} tandems are full and the rest pedal bicycles. Count the wheels.
test: {r} people, {t} full tandems, the rest one to a bike, {z} spectators watching. How many wheels?
test: {t} tandems all full n the rest on bikes, {r} of us. wheels?
test: {a} pumps up the tyres for {r} riders: {t} full tandems, everyone else rides solo on a bicycle. How many tyres?
exam: A party of {r} cyclists is conveyed upon {t} fully occupied tandems and individual bicycles, one rider per bicycle. Determine the aggregate number of wheels.
exam: Given that {r} riders are distributed such that {t.words} tandems are fully occupied and each remaining rider is mounted upon a separate bicycle, ascertain the number of wheels.
exam: Compute the number of tyres requiring inflation prior to the departure of {r} participants, of whom those not seated upon the {t} fully occupied tandems each ride a bicycle.
exam: It is stated that {r} persons hire cycles, {t} tandems being hired fully occupied and the remainder hiring bicycles singly. State the total number of wheels.
exercise: {r+1} riders signed up, but one "had a funny turn" at the start and went home. Of the other {r}, the riders on {t} tandems fill them and the rest ride a bicycle each. How many wheels are there?
exercise: {r+2} of us were gonna ride but 2 "had other commitments", aka couldn't be arsed. so {r}, {t} tandems full, rest on bikes. how many wheels
test: The organiser "massaged the numbers" and told the paper that {r*2} people took part. Really there were {r}: {t} full tandems and the rest one to a bicycle. How many wheels were really on the road?
